      "name": "Phoebetria",
      "rank": "GENUS",
      "description": "Sooty albatrosses — distinctive dark-plumaged albatrosses with long, wedge-shaped tails and a more gull-like flight. Found exclusively in the Southern Ocean. Their dark plumage may serve as camouflage against the dark seas of the stormy latitudes they inhabit.",
